--// HORROR MODE V10 - single LocalScript (client-side) with a lobby hub
--//
--// Where to put it: StarterPlayer -> StarterPlayerScripts -> LocalScript
--// (or run it with an executor - the script does not use anything from Explorer).
--//
--// Flow:    LOBBY (monster in the center, forest behind it)  ->  PLAY  ->  game
--//          STOP in the lobby stops the script, restores everything and deletes it.
--//          In game: [I] inventory has "QUIT TO LOBBY", or press [End].
--//
--// Architecture (everything is in this one file, but in separate layers):
--//   CORE  = gameplay mechanics: monster AI, stalking, damage, kills, items, difficulty.
--//           The core never touches sounds or UI directly - it only calls the FX API.
--//   FX    = client-side visuals and audio only: flashlight flicker, ambient sounds,
--//           hallucinations, fake footsteps, screen glitches, camera shake, jumpscares.
--//           FX never changes gameplay state, so you can switch any of it off in CONFIG.Features.
--//   NOTE: this is a client script, so nothing here is server-authoritative. For a real
--//           multiplayer game the CORE layer is the part you would move to a server Script.
--//
--// Every feature has a switch in CONFIG.Features and its own settings table.
--// Features the current game cannot support are disabled automatically (see "SUPPORT").

